WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.300
I'm Jenna Fisher, and I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是珍娜·费舍，我是安吉拉·金西。

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.140
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.280
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你打造了终极的《办公室》爱好者播客。

4
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.260
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office
每周，我们将深入探索《办公室》的世界

5
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.000
with exclusive interviews, behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
带来独家访谈、幕后细节以及大量闺蜜的故事。

6
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.000
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

7
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:26.870
Hi.
嗨。

8
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:27.870
How you doing?
你好吗？

9
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.170
I'm doing pretty good.
我挺好的。

10
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.570
I was doing pretty good, and then I just got a text, and now I'm in grumps.
我本来挺好的，然后我刚收到一条短信，现在我有点生气了。

11
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:34.770
Oh.
哦。

12
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.370
Can I tell you what it is?
能跟你说说是什么事吗？

13
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:36.770
Yeah.
行。

14
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.010
Because this is actually an opportunity for me to set something straight.
因为这其实是一个让我澄清某事的机会。

15
00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:40.750
Okay.
好的。

16
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.270
Am I coming in hot?
我是不是气势汹汹地进来的？

17
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.190
You're coming in a little spicy.
你现在火气有点大。

18
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:45.790
What you got?
有什么料？

19
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:46.710
All right.
好吧。

20
00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.710
Right before we got on mic, I'm checking my phone, and my mom has sent me this text,
就在我们开麦前，我查看手机，我妈给我发了这样一条短信

21
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:56.590
and she sent me this screenshot where she's like, facts about famous actresses.
她发给我一张截图，上面写着关于著名女演员的事实。

22
00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:57.230
Oh, no.
哦，不。

23
00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:57.850
I know.
我懂。

24
00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:58.730
Don't send me that.
别发给我这个。

25
00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.050
She's like, Jenna, I found this online.
她说，珍娜，我在网上看到的。

26
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:00.990
Is this true?
这是真的吗？

27
00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.110
Here's the fact about me.
下面是关于我的事实。

28
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:09.470
Jenna Fisher still owns the engagement ring her co-star, John Krasinski, gave her on The Office,
珍娜·费舍依然保留着她的搭档约翰·卡拉辛斯基在《办公室》里送给她的订婚戒指，

29
00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:12.470
and she has even been seen wearing it off screen.
甚至有人看到她在戏外戴着它。

30
00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.390
Everyone, settle down.
大家，冷静一下。

31
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.190
Not true.
这不是真的。

32
00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:24.630
I do have Pam's rings, which were, by the way, given to Pam from Jim, right?
我的确有潘的戒指，顺便说一句，那是吉姆送给潘的，对吧？

33
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:25.210
Yeah.
对。

34
00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.230
I also have Pam's purse.
我还有潘的钱包。

35
00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.450
I also have Pam's sweater.
我还拥有潘的毛衣。

36
00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.810
I have Pam's watch.
我有潘的手表。

37
00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:33.830
Who gave those items to you was the props department.
把这些物品交给你的是道具组。

38
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:34.970
Phil Shea.
菲尔·希亚。

39
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.770
Phil Shea, who also gave me my cat earrings that Angela Martin wore.
菲尔·希亚，他还给了我安吉拉·马丁戴过的小猫耳环。

40
00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:40.350
Yes.
没错。

41
00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:46.770
Phil Shea put together a wonderful package when the show ended of all of these iteMs.
剧集结束时，菲尔·希亚把所有这些物品打包成了一个精美的包裹送给我们。

42
00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:47.870
Pam's purse.
潘的钱包。

43
00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:52.930
I remember he gave John the satchel that Jim always carried.
我记得他把吉姆常背的那个斜挎包送给了约翰。

44
00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:53.870
The crossbody bag.
那个斜挎包。

45
00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:54.490
The crossbody bag.
那个斜挎包。

46
00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:57.190
So he collected little items for us.
所以他为我们收集了一些小物件。

47
00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.410
He gave me Dwight and Angela's wedding program.
他给了我德怀特和安吉拉的婚礼节目单。

48
00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:00.050
Yes.
是的。

49
00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:04.390
You have the ring that Dwight gives Angela.
你有德怀特送给安吉拉的那枚戒指。

50
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:04.990
Right.
对。

51
00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:05.550
Yes.
是的。

52
00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.790
So yes, I have this ring.
所以是的，我有这枚戒指。

53
00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.690
I have it along with many other items that I have.
我身上有很多其他东西，这只是其中之一。

54
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:16.190
There's nothing attached to it other than memorabilia from a show you were on that you loved.
上面除了你曾经深爱过的一个节目的纪念品之外，什么也没有。

55
00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:16.730
Correct.
没错。

56
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:17.150
Correct.
没错。

57
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:23.430
And you know what ring I wear is my actual wedding ring from my actual real-life husband
你知道我戴的是什么戒指吗？那是我现实生活中结婚16年的丈夫送的真结婚戒指

58
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.050
of 16 years, who I love with all my heart.
我爱他胜过一切。

59
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:27.670
Yes.
是的。

60
00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:29.430
Yes.
是的。

61
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.190
Sometimes it's just so hard, lady.
有时真的太难了，女士。

62
00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.210
The internet's a wackadoodle place.
互联网真是个古怪的地方。

63
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:34.970
It is.
确实如此。

64
00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.390
And I told you my crazy story.
我跟你讲过我那个疯狂的故事。

65
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.730
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

66
00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:39.250
You guys.
你们大家。

67
00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:39.930
This is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

68
00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.590
This story is so crazy.
这个故事太疯狂了。

69
00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.050
Sam, you don't know this story, but it's bonkers.
萨姆，你还不知道这个故事，但它简直离谱。

70
00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.050
You got to hear this.
你得听听这个。

71
00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.570
I told Jenna this the other day.
我前几天刚跟珍娜说过这事。

72
00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:47.390
Okay.
好吧。

73
00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:54.310
So you guys know I did a charity tennis match with Steve Carell, his wife, Nancy, and Rain
所以你们知道我参加了一场慈善网球赛，同行的有史蒂夫·卡瑞尔、他的妻子南希以及雷恩

74
00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:54.690
Wilson.
威尔逊。

75
00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:59.350
And it was all to go towards supporting Rain's amazing charity, Lidde Haiti.
这一切都是为了支持雷恩了不起的慈善机构Lidde Haiti。

76
00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.070
And after the tennis match, there was like a little meet and greet.
网球赛结束后，有一个小型见面会。

77
00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:07.050
And this man was there and he had sort of like an assistant person with him.
当时有个人在那里，他身边好像还跟着个助手似的人。

78
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.810
He was lovely, by the way.
顺便说一句，他人很好。

79
00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.630
But you could tell he was very excited that he had found different little pieces of trivia
但你能看出他非常激动，因为他在网上找到了关于我们的各种小冷门知识

80
00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.910
about us online.
。

81
00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.530
Again, it's the trivia.
又是这些小知识。

82
00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:22.110
It's the trivia, which is probably just an AI bot that gets half the information, right?
就是这些冷知识，大概只是某个AI机器人抓取了一半的信息吧？

83
00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.770
And then the rest is wrong.
然后剩下的全都是错的。

84
00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:23.990
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

85
00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.710
So like, I forget the information that he knew about Steve.
所以，我忘了关于史蒂夫他知道的那些信息是什么了。

86
00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.170
It was something like, oh, maybe his parents, how they met or something.
好像是关于他的父母，他们是怎么认识的之类的。

87
00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.110
I can't remember, right?
我记不清了，对吧？

88
00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.590
And Steve was like, oh yeah, that's correct.
史蒂夫就说，哦对，没错。

89
00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.550
Because probably he talked about it in an interview somewhere, right?
因为他大概在某个采访里说过这事吧？

90
00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.290
And then he turns to me and he goes, Angela, your family collects body parts?
然后他转向我问，安吉拉，你们家收集身体部位吗？

91
00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:44.630
Exactly.
完全正确。

92
00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.330
So I started laughing like that.
所以我开始这样大笑。

93
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.770
I said, what?
我说，什么？

94
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.230
I thought it was a joke.
我以为这是个玩笑。

95
00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.150
I thought I was getting punked somehow.
我以为自己被恶搞了。

96
00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.310
I was like, what?
我就问，什么？

97
00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:58.310
And then Steve literally was taking a sip of water and almost spit it all over me.
然后史蒂夫当时正喝着水，差点全喷到我身上。

98
00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.890
He started laughing so hard.
他笑得前俯后仰。

99
00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.450
And we looked at each other and I was like, what are you talking about?
我们对视了一眼，我问，你在说什么呢？

100
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:07.810
He turns to his assistant like, and she goes, the foot?
他转向他的助理说，然后助理回答，那个脚？

101
00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.590
And he goes, there was a foot that you guys had?
然后他说，你们以前是不是有个脚的模型？

102
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.930
Like a foot?
就那种脚？

103
00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.450
I was like, oh my gosh.
当时我就想，哦天哪。

104
00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:21.490
I said, you guys, you know how at Halloween you can go into Spencer's Gifts in the mall?
我说，伙计们，你们知道万圣节时你可以去商场里的斯宾塞礼品店吗？

105
00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.730
Yeah, get like a foot that hangs out of the trunk.
对，买那种挂在后备箱外面的脚。

106
00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.310
Get a foot that hangs out of the trunk.
买一只挂在后备箱外面的脚。

107
00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.210
Ha, ha, ha.
哈，哈，哈。

108
00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.670
My mom got one of those.
我妈妈就买了一个。

109
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:33.610
And instead of hanging it out of the trunk of the car, she put it by the bathroom door,
她没有把它挂在汽车后备箱外面，而是把它放在浴室门旁边，

110
00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.810
by our back door as like a prank.
放在我们后门旁边当作恶作剧。

111
00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.370
And we all were like, ah, and we were like, mom.
然后我们所有人都啊的一声，然后我们就说，妈妈。

112
00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.150
And it was a story I told where they were like, who's the prankster in your family?
这是我讲过的一个故事，当时他们问，你们家谁最喜欢恶作剧？

113
00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.890
I'm like, my mom was kind of a prankster.
我说，我妈妈其实挺爱搞恶作剧的。

114
00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:44.790
I told this one story.
我讲了这个故事。

115
00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:49.990
I'm like, oh my gosh, are there people somewhere in the world that think I have like a foot
我说，天哪，世界上会不会有人觉得我家里有个脚的模型

116
00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.030
in a jar that we collect this crap?
放在罐子里，我们专门收集这种破烂？

117
00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:56.710
But now all I can think about is, oh my God, now I've told the story here.
但现在我脑子里想的全是，哦天哪，现在我在这里把这个故事讲出来了。

118
00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.310
Now AI is going to take this.
现在人工智能要把这个录进去了。

119
00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.950
This is going to go into a transcript.
这将会变成一份文字记录。

120
00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.130
The story is out there in a second way.
这个故事以另一种方式传出去了。

121
00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.010
But I'm hoping, I want to set the record straight.
但我希望，我想澄清事实。

122
00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:09.350
AI, if you're listening, will you please stop telling this story about me?
人工智能，如果你在听，请你别再讲我这个故事了好吗？

123
00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:14.310
Because I've read this multiple times over the years, ever since I was on a talk show.
因为这些年来我读到过好多次，自从我上过一个脱口秀节目之后。

124
00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.850
And I gave a list of things that I kept from the show.
当时我列出了一份我在节目中保留下来的东西的清单。

125
00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:19.650
And this was one of the things in the liSt.
而这就是清单上的东西之一。

126
00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:24.210
And somehow the telephone game has turned this into something else.
不知怎么的，以讹传讹把这事变成别的东西了。

127
00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:25.890
Here's the thing I'm going to say.
我要说的是这个。

128
00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.910
If you're going to have an AI bot get something horribly wrong,
如果你非要让一个人工智能机器人把事情搞得离谱错漏，

129
00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:33.330
maybe the jewelry tidbit is better than the like collects body parts.
也许珠宝的八卦总比收集身体部位要好一点。

130
00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:34.350
Can we just say that?
我们能这么说吗？

131
00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.910
It does make me feel a little better.
这确实让我感觉好受了一点。

132
00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.390
I haven't told my mom the story, you guys, but I feel like I need to.
伙计们，我还没把这事告诉我妈，但我觉得我得告诉她。

133
00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:45.090
Because I feel like there's going to be someone at church that comes up to her and is like,
因为我觉得教会里会有人走到她面前对她说，

134
00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.630
Birdie, what's up with you and this foot?
伯蒂，你和这只脚是怎么回事？

135
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.210
What's with the feet?
这些脚是怎么回事？

136
00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:54.590
Well, Angela, I do appreciate you telling that story because I had the grumps and now I'm laughing.
好吧，安吉拉，我很感激你讲了那个故事，因为我刚才心情很郁闷，现在我笑出来了。

137
00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.470
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

138
00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.250
You're welcome.
不客气。

139
00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.390
And I'm actually really excited about our episode today.
而且我实际上对我们今天的这期节目感到非常兴奋。

140
00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:00.910
I'm happy to be here.
很高兴能来到这里。

141
00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:05.410
We get to talk with Calvin Tenor, who played Glenn in The Warehouse.
我们采访到了卡尔文·特纳，他在《仓库》里饰演格伦。

142
00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:09.710
You guys, he is just an absolute joyful person.
伙计们，他真的是一个绝对充满快乐的人。

143
00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.450
And I really can't wait for you all to get to know him better.
我真的迫不及待地想让大家更深入地了解他。

144
00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:18.350
And I've been reunited with him now over the last few years working on the AT&T commercial campaign.
而且在过去的几年里，因为合作AT&T的广告宣传活动，我和他又重聚了。

145
00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:22.850
So I'm just excited I get to see him again today because he just is wonderful.
所以我很高兴今天能再次见到他，因为他真的很棒。

146
00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:23.350
Same.
我也是。

147
00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:24.610
Jenna and I were really fortunate.
詹娜和我都非常幸运。

148
00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:30.270
We got to hang out and spend a lot of time with him over the past couple of years between fan conventions and AT&T.
在过去的两年里，从粉丝见面会到AT&T，我们有很多机会和他一起闲逛、共度时光。

149
00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.490
And you're going to see why we love him.
你们会明白为什么我们这么喜欢他。

150
00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:33.230
You just wait.
你们就拭目以待吧。

151
00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:37.030
But let's start with our fan chit chat question of the week.
但我们先从本周的粉丝闲聊问题开始。

152
00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.570
This is coming from Emily A.
这个问题来自亚利桑那州

153
00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.830
in Tucson, Arizona.
图森市的艾米丽·A。

154
